---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Case studies – B&G Engineering"
  description="Anonymized engineering examples for manufacturing, special-purpose machines, fixtures, jigs, DFM and prototyping tasks."
>
  <section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">Case studies</p>
    <h1>Practical engineering examples from manufacturing environments.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This page uses short anonymized examples to show the types of mechanical design,
      manufacturing-support and prototyping tasks B&G Engineering can support.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="case-grid">
    <article class="case-card">
      <p class="case-meta">Fixture / jig · manufacturing support</p>
      <h2>Simpler and more usable production fixture concept</h2>
      <p>
        For an existing production task, the goal was to improve positioning, clamping and operator usability.
        The focus was not a complex new machine, but a practical manufacturing-focused fixture concept.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>review of starting geometry and manufacturing constraints,</li>
        <li>clarification of positioning and clamping principles,</li>
        <li>preparation of CAD model and manufacturing-focused documentation.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="case-card">
      <p class="case-meta">DFM / DFA · design review</p>
      <h2>Manufacturability review before prototyping</h2>
      <p>
        A planned part or assembly was reviewed before prototyping.
        The goal was to reduce unnecessary manufacturing risks, difficult access points and overly tight or unjustified design details.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>review of critical dimensions, access and assembly sequence,</li>
        <li>identification of details that could be simplified,</li>
        <li>recommendations for a more manufacturing-friendly design.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="case-card">
      <p class="case-meta">Legacy documentation · CAD / drawings</p>
      <h2>Organizing incomplete technical documentation</h2>
      <p>
        When old drawings, existing parts or incomplete documentation are available, the first need is often not new design,
        but organizing the technical basis. This supports manufacturability, supplier communication and later modifications.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>organizing existing drawings, measurements and reference information,</li>
        <li>preparation of CAD model or updated manufacturing drawing,</li>
        <li>marking missing or uncertain technical information.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-box">
    <h2>Have a similar task?</h2>
    <p>
      Send a short description of the task, available drawings or CAD data, and the required timeline.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/en/contact/">Contact</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/en/services/">Services</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
